  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245974/assets/177d2949118515d96b6a1c49d0222a2417ab6236e8641f8d89c0cd8f6b30a592.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x$ has no horizontal asymptote. However, it does have the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Substituting $x=10$ into the equation of the curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(10) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1}) \\\\  & =1\\ne 100\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement I is true.",
